{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqf9rujm41b","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"judge journal test lags shadow classifier contract","summary":"test/judge-journal.test.js v2 blocks fail NOT from the DG1/DG2 claim gate but from a separate product change: commit 4f4e446 made appendVerdict() COMPUTE shadow_verdict/shadow_conf/model_version from the learned classifier (lib/judge.js shadowFields -> scripts/edge-clf-predict) instead of passing through the row's explicit values. With a classifier file present (.graph/edge-clf/v1.json modified), getClf() loads, so shadow fields are injected on EVERY journal row and model_version is always 'v1-provisional'. The test still asserts the old pass-through contract (explicit shadow_conf 0.72, model_version 'sonnet-4-6', and shadow fields ABSENT on legacy rows). Fix = update the test to the classifier-computed contract (shadow_verdict in keep/prune, shadow_conf numeric, model_version 'v1-provisional' when classifier loadable). Not a product bug.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T13:49:19.330Z","vec":[-0.08495547622442245,0.000279906700598076,-0.04638037830591202,-0.007551596965640783,0.07406590133905411,-0.07822856307029724,-0.0484306663274765,0.007849267683923244,-0.03237348794937134,0.058284491300582886,0.05330650135874748,0.004125376231968403,-0.008869717828929424,-0.021101677790284157,0.024449501186609268,0.09604258090257645,0.04418831318616867,0.011589938774704933,-0.029956499114632607,0.03353366255760193,-0.01389976218342781,0.019084550440311432,0.0181359201669693,0.014219189062714577,0.012698986567556858,-0.06598041206598282,-0.09207331389188766,0.04178741201758385,0.02594025246798992,-0.1445298194885254,0.03350498527288437,0.07017374038696289,-0.1289558708667755,0.0031373966485261917,0.07526129484176636,-0.034420810639858246,-0.007826901972293854,-0.0175027959048748,-0.017742088064551353,0.03958454355597496,0.03786483034491539,0.0035560671240091324,-0.0681404247879982,-0.014017404057085514,0.07506